Good — here's a live model you can drive yourself. Drag the frequency slider and every readout recomputes instantly.

**The model in one line:** seats offered per hour = buses per hour × seats per bus. Seats *available* (surplus) = offered − passengers per hour.

```openui lifecycle=ephemeral id=bus-frequency-seats

root = LearningSurface([expl, sim], "Bus frequency vs. seats available per hour", "Change the frequency and watch capacity recompute.", "ephemeral")
expl = Explanation("Three numbers drive everything:\n\n- **Buses per hour** — the frequency you control\n- **Seats per bus** — the capacity of one vehicle\n- **Passengers per hour** — the demand you must serve\n\n**Seats offered per hour** = buses/hour × seats/bus\n**Seats available (surplus)** = seats offered − passengers/hour\n**Capacity used** = passengers/hour ÷ seats offered\n\nIf surplus turns negative, some passengers are left standing: frequency is below what the demand needs.", "How the readouts are computed")
buses = { id: "busesPerHour", label: "Buses per hour", unit: "buses", min: 1, max: 60, step: 1, value: 10 }
seats = { id: "seatsPerBus", label: "Seats per bus", unit: "seats", min: 10, max: 90, step: 1, value: 40 }
riders = { id: "passengersPerHour", label: "Passengers per hour", unit: "people", min: 0, max: 3000, step: 50, value: 600 }
params = [buses, seats, riders]
offered = { id: "seatsOffered", label: "Seats offered per hour", unit: "seats", expr: "busesPerHour * seatsPerBus", precision: 0 }
surplus = { id: "seatsAvailable", label: "Seats available per hour (surplus)", unit: "seats", expr: "busesPerHour * seatsPerBus - passengersPerHour", precision: 0, emphasis: true }
util = { id: "capacityUsed", label: "Capacity used", unit: "%", expr: "passengersPerHour / (busesPerHour * seatsPerBus) * 100", precision: 1 }
spare = { id: "sparesPerBus", label: "Spares per bus (avg)", unit: "seats", expr: "seatsPerBus - passengersPerHour / busesPerHour", precision: 1 }
need = { id: "busesToServe", label: "Buses needed if each runs full", unit: "buses", expr: "passengersPerHour / seatsPerBus", precision: 1 }
readouts = [offered, surplus, util, spare, need]
sim = Simulation("bus-freq-seats", "Bus frequency vs. seats available per hour", params, readouts, "ephemeral", "Before you move anything: what do you predict the surplus to be if you double the frequency from 10 to 20 buses per hour? Then drag the frequency slider and check. Try a second move that pushes the surplus negative, and watch capacity used climb past 100%. When you're done, press 'Share what I found' so I can see your settings and readouts.")

```

Two things worth exploring once you start moving it: whether doubling frequency doubles the surplus (it doesn't — surplus only doubles if demand is zero), and where the break-even point sits, where surplus hits exactly zero.

When you've played with it, hit **Share what I found** and I'll work through your actual numbers with you.
